      "created_at": "2018-01-08T18:01:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-01-08T18:01:13Z",
      "body": "In Google Tag Manager, I have added the Google Analytics `anonymizeIp : true` property.  I verified that the IP anonymization property is enabled by looking for `aip=1` in the google analytics traffic on openliberty.io.\r\n\r\nExample of verification:\r\n1.  Open new tab in Chrome\r\n2.  Enable Chrome debug tools\r\n3.  In tools, open the Network tab\r\n4.  Go to openliberty.io\r\n5.  Filter the network data with the word `analytics`\r\n6.  Observe that the `collect` request has the `aip=1`, meaning IP addresses are anonymized.\r\n\r\n> The IP anonymization parameter looks like this: &aip=1\r\n> src: https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/2763052?hl=en&ref_topic=2919631",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
